# Trivy has its own ignore mechanism, separate from pnpm audit's
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml` -> `auditConfig.ignoreGhsas`. These three entries
# mirror decisions already made and documented there — same CVEs, same
# reasoning, kept consistent across both scanners:
#
# CVE-2026-59892 (GHSA-45rx-2jwx-cxfr): @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger DoS
# via malformed HTTP header. Deep in the OpenTelemetry SDK bundle shared
# across auth-service/portfolio-api/portfolio-service/price-processor/
# profile-service; not overridden due to peer-dependency risk. Fix >=2.9.0.
CVE-2026-59892

# CVE-2026-59869 (GHSA-52cp-r559-cp3m): js-yaml v4 line DoS via merge-key
# chains, pulled in via eslint>@eslint/eslintrc>js-yaml. Not overridden:
# eslint's config loader may be pinned to a specific js-yaml major. Dev-only
# dep, not reachable in production. Fix >=4.3.0.
CVE-2026-59869

# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj: sharp's bundled libvips carries CVE-2026-33327/33328/
# 35590/35591. sharp is Next.js's image-processing binary; fix >=0.35.0.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj

# CVE-2026-14257 (GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg): brace-expansion DoS via unbounded
# expansion length, pulled in ~100 paths deep through glob>minimatch in
# @opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node and @sentry/nextjs's bundler
# plugins — build-time/instrumentation tooling only. Fix >=5.0.8. Mirrors
# pnpm-workspace.yaml's ignoreGhsas entry added 2026-07-26.
CVE-2026-14257

# GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849: postcss path traversal via auto-loaded
# sourceMappingURL, pulled in ~10 paths deep through @sentry/nextjs and
# next's own webpack toolchain — build-time CSS tooling only, never
# processes untrusted input at runtime. Fix >=8.5.18. Mirrors
# pnpm-workspace.yaml's ignoreGhsas entry added 2026-07-26.
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849
